(387770, 32267, 6349, '<td valign="top">I knew this was yours.  I''m back as I promised to add this to my favorites.  It seems that I have no idea what I''m talking about but I still think this should have gotten a ribbon.  You never cease to amaze me.  I was really surprised with your movie submission.  I thought it was excellent and never would have suspected it was yours.  I love to see a range in a persons work and your portfolio is a great example.</td>', 'I knew this was yours.  I''m back as I promised to add this to my favorites.  It seems that I have no idea what I''m talking about but I still think this should have gotten a ribbon.  You never cease to amaze me.  I was really surprised with your movie submission.  I thought it was excellent and never would have suspected it was yours.  I love to see a range in a persons work and your portfolio is a great example.', '2003-08-14 03:19:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(387774, 32359, 6349, '<td valign="top">A cynic''s view, naturally!  LOL.  Good statement.  I loved this photo in terms of the meanings created by the photos you put together.  I would have given this a 10 but I only gave it a 9 as there was something very unrealistic looking about it (whereas it could have looked very realistic).  Perhaps it was the placement of the city on such an abrupt higher angle.  Great work though, I was very impressed by the image itself and the thought process behind it.</td>', 'A cynic''s view, naturally!  LOL.  Good statement.  I loved this photo in terms of the meanings created by the photos you put together.  I would have given this a 10 but I only gave it a 9 as there was something very unrealistic looking about it (whereas it could have looked very realistic).  Perhaps it was the placement of the city on such an abrupt higher angle.  Great work though, I was very impressed by the image itself and the thought process behind it.', '2003-08-14 03:22:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(387791, 32267, 8987, '<td valign="top">Hi, could you please explain the reason you made that circle? Thanks.</td>', 'Hi, could you please explain the reason you made that circle? Thanks.', '2003-08-14 03:39:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(387792, 31875, 8987, '<td valign="top">For those wanting to know how you do this:<br/> <br/>I used a tripod with my camera and then, from exact the same position, I took three succeeding shots, my father always sitting differently on each one. Afterwards I merged them in Photoshop, did some fine tuning and voilà!<br/> <br/>As for those who thought the left was a bit too bright: Well, you aren''t completely wrong but I used a ''Diffuse Glow'' on the picture to make the surrounding a bit more surreal or futuristic.<br/> <br/>The other ''cloners'' have done a nice job too, especially Kiwiness! It''s hilarious :)</td>', 'For those wanting to know how you do this: I used a tripod with my camera and then, from exact the same position, I took three succeeding shots, my father always sitting differently on each one. Afterwards I merged them in Photoshop, did some fine tuning and voilà! As for those who thought the left was a bit too bright: Well, you aren''t completely wrong but I used a ''Diffuse Glow'' on the picture to make the surrounding a bit more surreal or futuristic. The other ''cloners'' have done a nice job too, especially Kiwiness! It''s hilarious :)', '2003-08-14 03:39:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(387800, 31875, 5728, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SoulHunter74:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>The other ''cloners'' have done a nice job too, especially Kiwiness! It''s hilarious :)</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, thanx for the compliment Jerome. This is also very good. Isn''t it surprising how many people had the same idea huh?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-08-14 02:48:35.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by SoulHunter74: The other ''cloners'' have done a nice job too, especially Kiwiness! It''s hilarious :)  Well, thanx for the compliment Jerome. This is also very good. Isn''t it surprising how many people had the same idea huh?', '2003-08-14 03:48:11.000000', '2003-08-14 03:48:35.000000', 0),
