(393200, 31981, 6202, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I have sat here for sometime trying to figure out what to say about this photo.  It would make a really good photo for action or sports but for future without the title it doesn''t work.<br/> <br/>your colors seem a little off you might need to adjust your white balance.  <br/> <br/>Overall the photo is not bad I see a lot of blurred movement but that is a good effect for the image in this case.  I just don''t see it fitting the challenge all that well.</td>', '*Critique Club* I have sat here for sometime trying to figure out what to say about this photo.  It would make a really good photo for action or sports but for future without the title it doesn''t work. your colors seem a little off you might need to adjust your white balance.   Overall the photo is not bad I see a lot of blurred movement but that is a good effect for the image in this case.  I just don''t see it fitting the challenge all that well.', '2003-08-19 21:12:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(394100, 31643, 6999, '<td valign="top">Hi from the CC, Betty.<br/> <br/>Ooh. Didn''t see this one - didn''t vote. I love the effect, but I would imagine you were done for taking this too far away from photography, and into more art areas. Whilst that was obviously within the rules, I still think people were looking for stuff that was more clearly photos. <br/> <br/>I''d be very interested to see the original - did it still manage to have that intensity of heat that you''ve caught with this? If so then I''d agree with the comment about the brush filter. <br/> <br/>It fots the challenge clearly though, and there''s certainly a quality to it that deserves far more than it''s score or placing. Without the greyness at the bottom of frme it would be nothing though - very well done there.<br/> <br/>Good luck<br/> <br/>Ed</td>', 'Hi from the CC, Betty. Ooh. Didn''t see this one - didn''t vote. I love the effect, but I would imagine you were done for taking this too far away from photography, and into more art areas. Whilst that was obviously within the rules, I still think people were looking for stuff that was more clearly photos.  I''d be very interested to see the original - did it still manage to have that intensity of heat that you''ve caught with this? If so then I''d agree with the comment about the brush filter.  It fots the challenge clearly though, and there''s certainly a quality to it that deserves far more than it''s score or placing. Without the greyness at the bottom of frme it would be nothing though - very well done there. Good luck Ed', '2003-08-20 10:56:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(394727, 32335, 6999, '<td valign="top">from the critique club, Hi Jimmy<br/> <br/>One of the best wedding photos I''ve ever seen. The detailing and contrat os first class - especially on the flowers. The highlighting of the rings is absolutely wonderful - this would win all sorts of competitions, I''m sure.<br/> <br/>The reason it didn''t win this one is because of the subject, obviously. Whilst it could quite happily be the future for many, it isn''t specifically so. Can''t say I''m sad about that - else you''d be way up above my shot :-)<br/> <br/>Ed</td>', 'from the critique club, Hi Jimmy One of the best wedding photos I''ve ever seen. The detailing and contrat os first class - especially on the flowers. The highlighting of the rings is absolutely wonderful - this would win all sorts of competitions, I''m sure. The reason it didn''t win this one is because of the subject, obviously. Whilst it could quite happily be the future for many, it isn''t specifically so. Can''t say I''m sad about that - else you''d be way up above my shot :-) Ed', '2003-08-20 16:55:54.000000', NULL, 0),
